      "This batch introduces a new municipal-utility record (Riverside Public Utilities) confirmed via Riverside's absence from SCE's own service-area fact sheet, following the same pattern already established for Burbank, Glendale, and Anaheim in earlier batches.",
      "Corona was discovered this session to be genuinely split between SCE and the City's own Department of Water and Power (DWP), directly confirmed by the city's own Expedited Permits page naming both as possible providers depending on address. Because no majority-territory evidence could be found (unlike the street-level boundary evidence available for Laguna Niguel/Laguna Hills/Mission Viejo in Wave B), utility was left null rather than guessing a majority provider — a stricter application of the null-over-guess rule than the earlier split-territory pattern.",
      "Eastvale, Jurupa Valley, Norco, and Perris are all listed as Western Community Energy (WCE) member cities, but WCE deregistered with the CPUC and dissolved via Chapter 9 bankruptcy in 2021 with customers involuntarily returned to their default IOU. generation_supplier was left null for all four rather than recording a defunct CCA relationship as current — the same defunct-CCA handling already established for Lake Forest's OCPA withdrawal in Wave B."
